        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "20662083-8179-5769-9d39-3d2d011518c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Labrador Retriever, Tibetan Terrier, Mastador, Mastiff, Apso\n- People: Rudd Weatherwax, Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, Kevin Corcoran\n- Animals: Spike\n- Films and television: Old Yeller, Lassie\n- Concepts: retriever-gun dog, dog actor, working dog\n\nFacts:\n- The Labrador Retriever, also called the Labrador, is a type of retriever-gun dog.\n- Some old travelers' accounts refer to the Tibetan Terrier as Dokhi Apso or \"outdoor\" Apso, indicating a shaggy or bearded working dog that lives outdoors.\n- Rudd Weatherwax handled the dogs for the television series Lassie, which ran from 1954 to 1974.\n- In 1957, Rudd Weatherwax trained Spike for the feature film Old Yeller.\n- Spike was a lop-eared yellow Mastador, a Mastiff and Labrador Retriever mix.\n- Spike was a dog actor best known for playing Old Yeller in the 1957 Disney film Old Yeller, which co-starred Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, and Kevin Corcoran.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "670816a1-d695-581c-9330-6775046159eb",
        "text": "Page: Labrador Retriever. Sentence: The Labrador Retriever, also Labrador, is a type of retriever-gun dog.\nPage: Tibetan Terrier. Sentence: Some old travelers' accounts refer to the dog as Dokhi Apso or \"outdoor\" Apso, indicating a shaggy or bearded working dog which lives outdoors.\nPage: Spike (dog). Sentence: Spike was a lop-eared yellow Mastador (Mastiff/ Labrador Retriever mix) and a dog actor best known for his performance as Old Yeller in the 1957 Disney film of the same name co-starring Tommy Kirk, Dorothy McGuire, Fess Parker, and Kevin Corcoran.\nPage: Rudd Weatherwax. Sentence: He also handled the dogs for the \"Lassie\" television series which ran from 1954 to 1974, and trained Spike for the 1957 feature film \"Old Yeller\".",
